Treat a resource array length that is not a constant as unknown when computing binding ranges.

ExtendedTypeLayoutContext::addRangesRec (source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp), which builds the
binding ranges spReflectionTypeLayout_getBindingRangeCount and the other binding-range queries
report, multiplies the ranges of an array's element by the array's length:

    if (arrayType->isUnsized())
        elementCount = LayoutSize::infinite();
    else if (arrayType->getElementCount()->isLinkTimeVal())
        elementCount = LayoutSize::invalid();
    else
        elementCount = LayoutSize::RawValue(getIntVal(arrayType->getElementCount()));   // 2146

For Texture2D t[kCount] with kCount a specialization constant, the length is a DeclRefIntVal that
is not a link-time value, so getIntVal is reached and raises SLANG_UNEXPECTED
(source/slang/slang-syntax.cpp:898-905). The Slang::InternalError leaves the extern "C" query: a
structured exception on Windows, std::terminate (SIGABRT) on Linux and macOS, from the first
binding-range query on the scope. slangc -reflection-json stops the same way on such a shader,
while slangc -target spirv compiles it. The array's own layout already treats any length that is
not a ConstantIntVal as unknown (GetElementCount in source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp:3085-3128).

This takes the length of a ConstantIntVal and LayoutSize::invalid() for any other, as the link-time
case already did, so the binding range is reported with a binding count of SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE. A
constant length, an unsized array and a link-time length give the ranges they gave before. A
regression test is added as
tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-specialization-sized-resource-array-reflection.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21 with Texture2D scArray[kCascades]; SamplerState scSampler;: before, the first
getBindingRangeCount on the global scope throws (win-x64: a structured exception; linux-x64:
SIGABRT); after, two binding ranges, the texture array's binding count SLANG_UNKNOWN_SIZE and the
sampler's 1 (win-x64, linux-x64).
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp b/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
index 3f7940272..9f83ff5fd 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
@@ -2147,10 +2147,17 @@ struct ExtendedTypeLayoutContext
             {
                 if (arrayType->isUnsized())
                     elementCount = LayoutSize::infinite();
-                else if (arrayType->getElementCount()->isLinkTimeVal())
-                    elementCount = LayoutSize::invalid();
+                else if (
+                    auto constantElementCount = as<ConstantIntVal>(arrayType->getElementCount()))
+                    elementCount = LayoutSize::RawValue(constantElementCount->getValue());
                 else
-                    elementCount = LayoutSize::RawValue(getIntVal(arrayType->getElementCount()));
+                {
+                    // An element count that is not a constant, such as a link-time constant
+                    // or a specialization constant, is not known until the program is linked
+                    // or specialized, as for the array's own layout (`GetElementCount` in
+                    // slang-type-layout.cpp).
+                    elementCount = LayoutSize::invalid();
+                }
             }
             addRangesRec(elementTypeLayout, path, multiplier * elementCount);
             return;
